Why Synchronization Is Needed?

Without synchronization:

Banking Errors

Wrong balances.

Database Corruption

Incorrect records.

File Corruption

Two processes writing simultaneously.

Operating System Failure

Shared kernel data corrupted.

Producer-Consumer Example

Classic Interview Problem.

Producer:

Creates Data

Consumer:

Uses Data

Shared Buffer:

[ ]

Problems:

Buffer Full

Producer must wait.

Buffer Empty

Consumer must wait.

Synchronization required.

Reader-Writer Example

Another famous problem.

Readers:

Only Read Data

Writers:

Modify Data

Multiple readers can read together.

But writer needs exclusive access.

Dining Philosophers Problem

Very famous interview question.

Five philosophers sit around a table.

Need two forks to eat.

Possible issue:

Everyone picks left fork.

Nobody gets right fork.

System gets stuck.

This introduces:

Deadlock

which we'll study later.

Software Solutions (Historical)

Early synchronization used algorithms like:

Peterson's Algorithm

Two-process synchronization algorithm.

Interview concept.

Rarely used practically today.

Hardware Solutions

Modern CPUs provide atomic instructions.

Examples:

Test-and-Set
Compare-and-Swap

Used to build locks.

