Interview Questions
Q1. What is Process Synchronization?

Answer:

Coordinating processes/threads so shared data remains consistent.

Q2. What is Race Condition?

Answer:

When multiple threads access shared data simultaneously causing unpredictable results.

Q3. What is Critical Section?

Answer:

Code section where shared resources are accessed.

Q4. What is Mutual Exclusion?

Answer:

Only one thread/process may enter critical section at a time.

Q5. Why Is Synchronization Needed?

Answer:

To prevent data inconsistency and race conditions.

